1
00:00:13,993 --> 00:00:17,038
OUR STICKY LOVE

2
00:00:25,839 --> 00:00:26,673
Chairman, sir.

3
00:00:27,674 --> 00:00:29,759
Prosecutor Go isn't on the cargo ship.

4
00:00:36,432 --> 00:00:37,892
Baek Sang-gil!

5
00:01:09,174 --> 00:01:11,092
So we meet like this.

6
00:01:12,385 --> 00:01:14,012
I used to call you Coach.

7
00:01:15,388 --> 00:01:17,056
But what should I call you now?

8
00:01:18,391 --> 00:01:21,019
There isn't really a way
for an abandoned disciple

9
00:01:21,519 --> 00:01:22,979
to address their master.

10
00:01:25,106 --> 00:01:26,858
1991 NATIONAL BOXING TEAM
FINAL SELECTION

11
00:01:26,941 --> 00:01:28,860
LIGHT WELTERWEIGHT MATCHUP

12
00:01:28,943 --> 00:01:30,695
BAEK SANG-GIL
VS LEE JUNG-GU

13
00:01:32,322 --> 00:01:34,991
Baek Sang-gil is in great form today.

14
00:01:35,074 --> 00:01:38,494
At this rate, Baek Sang-gil's gold medal
is almost guaranteed.

15
00:01:41,164 --> 00:01:41,998
No holding.

16
00:01:45,585 --> 00:01:47,337
Baek Sang-gil is really going for it.

17
00:01:53,885 --> 00:01:55,845
No holding. Break!

18
00:02:00,433 --> 00:02:01,559
Stop!

19
00:02:04,854 --> 00:02:05,855
What's going on here?

20
00:02:05,939 --> 00:02:06,981
Blue corner.

21
00:02:07,065 --> 00:02:08,358
You forfeit. It's over.

22
00:02:08,441 --> 00:02:12,070
Baek Sang-gil's coach
just threw in the towel.

23
00:02:12,153 --> 00:02:15,782
It's not uncommon for a coach
to throw in the towel

24
00:02:15,865 --> 00:02:17,951
to protect their fighter at risk.

25
00:02:18,034 --> 00:02:20,662
But, in this case,
Baek Sang-gil had the upper hand.

26
00:02:20,745 --> 00:02:22,872
-Exactly.
-It's a little baffling.

27
00:02:22,956 --> 00:02:25,750
Baek Sang-gil also looks
very confused right now.

28
00:02:27,961 --> 00:02:29,045
Coach!

29
00:02:30,672 --> 00:02:32,048
What the heck did you…

30
00:02:33,424 --> 00:02:34,425
Take them off.

31
00:02:41,432 --> 00:02:43,893
Thought I wouldn't hear
the difference in your gloves?

32
00:02:45,853 --> 00:02:49,774
I had it in the bag. I was so close
to becoming a national athlete.

33
00:02:49,857 --> 00:02:53,319
You think you can become
a national athlete with such dirty fists?

34
00:02:53,403 --> 00:02:55,905
Wouldn't it be good for you
if I make the national team?

35
00:02:57,991 --> 00:03:00,994
Taking you in as my disciple,
even for a short time,

36
00:03:01,077 --> 00:03:03,288
will have been
the most shameful thing in my life.

37
00:03:03,371 --> 00:03:06,124
-Coach!
-From this moment on, I'm not your coach.

38
00:03:06,916 --> 00:03:09,294
I never taught you
to use your fists to harm others.

39
00:03:14,757 --> 00:03:16,050
Fuck this!

40
00:03:18,511 --> 00:03:22,181
I cherish Jang Tae-ha as if he were made
from my own rib.

41
00:03:22,849 --> 00:03:25,310
And soon, not only me

42
00:03:25,393 --> 00:03:30,440
but all of Korea will come to cherish him
as a great athlete.

43
00:03:45,621 --> 00:03:49,208
Your disciple who wound up on
the same path as me, whom you despised.

44
00:03:50,293 --> 00:03:52,754
I'm sure it wasn't easy to take him back.

45
00:03:52,837 --> 00:03:55,882
I'm truly sorry
things turned out this way.

46
00:03:56,883 --> 00:03:57,800
You know what?

47
00:04:10,980 --> 00:04:13,900
The thrill of throwing punches
with your life on the line

48
00:04:14,692 --> 00:04:18,988
makes those pretty little jabs in the ring
pale in comparison.

49
00:04:23,284 --> 00:04:25,661
Even after 30 years,

50
00:04:27,538 --> 00:04:30,333
you haven't changed one bit,
Baek Sang-gil.

51
00:04:32,585 --> 00:04:34,087
Do you think you corrupted

52
00:04:35,046 --> 00:04:36,506
someone I care about?

53
00:04:38,257 --> 00:04:39,175
You didn't.

54
00:04:40,051 --> 00:04:41,052
Tae-ha

55
00:04:41,719 --> 00:04:43,304
has never been corrupted.

56
00:04:44,931 --> 00:04:48,768
Even now, you're trying
to kill innocent folks for your own greed.

57
00:04:49,268 --> 00:04:51,938
But Tae-ha did all this
to save someone's life.

58
00:04:55,149 --> 00:04:56,359
So

59
00:04:57,276 --> 00:04:59,070
you've got nothing to be proud of.

60
00:05:08,079 --> 00:05:12,166
I reported a car explosion,
so the police will be here soon.

61
00:05:12,959 --> 00:05:15,253
If you have the guts,
stay and see what happens.

62
00:05:52,415 --> 00:05:53,541
Tae-ha.

63
00:05:55,084 --> 00:05:55,960
Are you okay?

64
00:05:58,379 --> 00:05:59,422
Can you get up?

65
00:05:59,922 --> 00:06:00,923
Try to get up.

66
00:06:13,519 --> 00:06:16,147
I told you not to get involved.

67
00:06:16,647 --> 00:06:18,232
Why did you come?

68
00:06:18,316 --> 00:06:23,029
Even if you had Gang-rok, the gas cans,
and were ready to call the police,

69
00:06:23,112 --> 00:06:26,240
what if something went wrong?
How could you go at him like that?

70
00:06:27,950 --> 00:06:31,037
Still… Go Eun-sae got away.

71
00:06:33,873 --> 00:06:34,790
Safely.

72
00:06:36,209 --> 00:06:37,877
She got away safely.

73
00:06:44,383 --> 00:06:46,969
No, Jang Tae-ha!

74
00:07:02,443 --> 00:07:03,569
Tae-ha.

75
00:07:04,278 --> 00:07:05,196
Tae-ha!

76
00:07:05,279 --> 00:07:07,448
Stay with me. Tae-ha!

77
00:07:08,032 --> 00:07:10,034
Hey, stay with me! Tae-ha!

78
00:07:22,129 --> 00:07:23,965
-Let go.
-I won't. We have to go.

79
00:07:24,048 --> 00:07:25,508
I have to go now!

80
00:07:25,591 --> 00:07:26,759
If you do, you'll die.

81
00:07:26,842 --> 00:07:28,386
I said let go of me!

82
00:07:29,178 --> 00:07:30,179
Step on their foot,

83
00:07:30,263 --> 00:07:31,222
trip them up,

84
00:07:31,305 --> 00:07:32,181
and run away.

85
00:07:44,527 --> 00:07:45,820
Ms. Go Eun-sae!

86
00:07:46,612 --> 00:07:47,446
Damn it.

87
00:08:12,972 --> 00:08:14,765
I'M DONE
LEAVE AT THE COAST GUARD SIREN

88
00:08:19,937 --> 00:08:21,355
What the… Eun-sae?

89
00:08:24,191 --> 00:08:25,359
Kaito?

90
00:09:24,585 --> 00:09:27,546
Just don't disappear without a word.
Just stay out of danger.

91
00:09:27,630 --> 00:09:28,756
Just…

92
00:09:30,508 --> 00:09:32,176
Just stay safe.

93
00:10:43,956 --> 00:10:44,790
Park Hyo-jin.

94
00:10:48,836 --> 00:10:50,087
You bitch.

95
00:11:03,684 --> 00:11:04,894
Is it back?

96
00:11:05,519 --> 00:11:06,520
Your memory?

97
00:11:09,231 --> 00:11:10,232
Yeah,

98
00:11:11,192 --> 00:11:12,610
you bitch.

99
00:11:32,922 --> 00:11:34,548
What's with the bag of taffy?

100
00:11:35,299 --> 00:11:37,802
All I knew was
that you were in some taffy village,

101
00:11:37,885 --> 00:11:39,720
so what else could I do?

102
00:11:40,513 --> 00:11:45,017
You deleted your Instagram account,
and I lost your new phone number.

103
00:11:46,811 --> 00:11:49,063
Why bother searching for a bitch
you hate so much?

104
00:11:49,146 --> 00:11:52,566
If you got your revenge,
you should've moved on for good.

105
00:11:53,692 --> 00:11:55,694
You don't even have the guts to do that.

106
00:11:59,156 --> 00:12:00,866
It all came back to me.

107
00:12:19,885 --> 00:12:21,470
Hey, switch shoes with me.

108
00:12:24,598 --> 00:12:25,724
Hey.

109
00:12:52,418 --> 00:12:53,794
The hurt kept piling up,

110
00:12:54,503 --> 00:12:57,256
and I'd forgotten about
all the good times we'd shared.

111
00:12:57,756 --> 00:13:00,134
But after I got my revenge on you,

112
00:13:01,176 --> 00:13:03,888
all the hurt disappeared,
and I could see it again.

113
00:13:05,264 --> 00:13:06,724
The good times we had.

114
00:13:08,475 --> 00:13:11,312
And the sort of friend you used to be.

115
00:13:13,981 --> 00:13:14,899
I'm sorry.

116
00:13:14,982 --> 00:13:16,817
I lived my life wrong.

117
00:13:17,985 --> 00:13:19,862
I'm really sorry.

118
00:13:20,362 --> 00:13:21,572
It's okay.

119
00:13:22,907 --> 00:13:24,241
I'm sorry for everything.

120
00:13:24,325 --> 00:13:25,993
I'm more sorry.

121
00:13:26,076 --> 00:13:29,121
No. I'm even more sorry.

122
00:13:38,672 --> 00:13:40,674
Eun-sae, drink this while it's warm.

123
00:13:40,758 --> 00:13:42,009
Thanks.

124
00:13:48,390 --> 00:13:49,892
Where were you, really?

125
00:13:51,936 --> 00:13:52,770
Gujin.

126
00:13:53,646 --> 00:13:56,690
Gujin? Right, Gujin.

127
00:13:57,358 --> 00:13:59,568
So there's a taffy village there too.

128
00:14:00,110 --> 00:14:04,782
And who was the person who took you in?

129
00:14:11,497 --> 00:14:15,709
He was… someone that I knew.

130
00:14:17,086 --> 00:14:19,004
What's your name?

131
00:14:19,838 --> 00:14:21,548
Jang Tae-ha.

132
00:14:21,632 --> 00:14:23,884
We had met before,

133
00:14:23,968 --> 00:14:26,887
and he was someone
who left me with a good memory.

134
00:14:26,971 --> 00:14:29,014
But I like this one the most.

135
00:14:29,098 --> 00:14:30,724
I met my first love here.

136
00:14:30,808 --> 00:14:31,976
It was nice meeting you,

137
00:14:32,059 --> 00:14:33,811
Mr. Future Gold Medalist.

138
00:14:35,270 --> 00:14:36,397
And it turned out

139
00:14:36,480 --> 00:14:39,400
that we'd first crossed paths
a very long time ago.

140
00:14:46,323 --> 00:14:49,201
MIRAE EDEN COMPANY
ORGANIZATIONAL CHART

141
00:14:49,284 --> 00:14:50,911
JANG TAE-HA
DIRECTOR

142
00:14:50,995 --> 00:14:53,372
I'm sorry that I was

143
00:14:54,331 --> 00:14:55,290
a gangster.

144
00:14:55,374 --> 00:14:57,751
He was an unfortunate person

145
00:14:57,835 --> 00:15:00,087
who lived a life he never wanted.

146
00:15:00,587 --> 00:15:01,422
It's me.

147
00:15:01,922 --> 00:15:03,257
Jang Tae-ha.

148
00:15:03,340 --> 00:15:04,675
Your boyfriend.

149
00:15:06,010 --> 00:15:07,344
We met in the mountains.

150
00:15:07,428 --> 00:15:10,389
Our dog isn't in the yard.

151
00:15:10,472 --> 00:15:12,850
I'll hurry and go find her.

152
00:15:15,978 --> 00:15:18,439
He even put on a clumsy act.

153
00:15:18,522 --> 00:15:20,190
Don't take it too hard.

154
00:15:20,691 --> 00:15:22,776
If you keep living…

155
00:15:27,865 --> 00:15:29,366
everything passes.

156
00:15:47,468 --> 00:15:49,386
He's the one who saved me.

157
00:15:52,306 --> 00:15:53,640
Eun-sae.

158
00:15:56,685 --> 00:16:01,190
He risked his life to save me
until the very end.

159
00:16:13,702 --> 00:16:14,870
What was that?

160
00:16:17,247 --> 00:16:20,125
You mean Prosecutor Go
didn't get on the boat?

161
00:16:20,209 --> 00:16:22,711
Then where is Eun-sae right now?

162
00:16:24,630 --> 00:16:25,464
I don't know.

163
00:16:26,465 --> 00:16:30,219
The last thing I saw
was her riding off on my motorcycle.

164
00:16:30,803 --> 00:16:33,347
-Good heavens.
-Goodness, what do we do?

165
00:16:33,931 --> 00:16:35,516
Tae-ha will freak if he finds out.

166
00:16:35,599 --> 00:16:38,852
But even if he does find out,
there's no way for us to find her.

167
00:16:38,936 --> 00:16:41,438
She turned her phone off,
and we can't just…

168
00:16:43,982 --> 00:16:46,527
ask the police for help either.

169
00:16:48,445 --> 00:16:50,447
Goodness. What are we gonna do?

170
00:16:58,455 --> 00:17:00,666
Let's not tell Tae-ha for now.

171
00:17:01,542 --> 00:17:03,836
If that punk finds out
she didn't get on the boat,

172
00:17:03,919 --> 00:17:08,132
he'll leave this place in a flash
and scour the entire country for her.

173
00:17:08,215 --> 00:17:10,384
-Yeah.
-Yes, I agree with you.

174
00:17:10,467 --> 00:17:13,470
Instead, I'll look into the facilities
across the country.

175
00:17:14,138 --> 00:17:16,223
Yeah, okay.

176
00:17:27,192 --> 00:17:28,318
Thank goodness.

177
00:17:29,403 --> 00:17:32,072
I'm so glad you had him.

178
00:17:35,367 --> 00:17:38,662
There's only one thing I can do
for Jang Tae-ha.

179
00:17:39,204 --> 00:17:40,831
I need to catch Baek Sang-gil.

180
00:17:41,915 --> 00:17:45,210
-You're going back to work?
-No, I need to see how things go first.

181
00:17:45,294 --> 00:17:47,087
If they put me on long-term leave,

182
00:17:47,171 --> 00:17:49,840
Baek Sang-gil must have people
in the Prosecutor's Office.

183
00:17:49,923 --> 00:17:53,051
Baek Sang-gil tortured me
to find out where my watch was.

184
00:17:53,135 --> 00:17:55,429
And in the end, he found it. I saw it.

185
00:17:56,597 --> 00:17:58,599
But even after finding it,
he didn't kill me.

186
00:17:58,682 --> 00:17:59,725
That means

187
00:17:59,808 --> 00:18:01,810
he knows about my plan B.

188
00:18:01,894 --> 00:18:03,854
And the only person who knows about that

189
00:18:03,937 --> 00:18:05,397
is Chi-hyeon.

190
00:18:06,899 --> 00:18:10,152
Actually, when I mentioned
that I was going to report you missing…

191
00:18:10,652 --> 00:18:11,570
She's not missing.

192
00:18:11,653 --> 00:18:14,198
…Chi-hyeon told me not to,
saying you weren't missing.

193
00:18:14,281 --> 00:18:17,242
But something felt off about it.

194
00:18:18,035 --> 00:18:19,494
Does that mean he's also…

195
00:18:19,578 --> 00:18:21,580
He's likely to be one of them.

196
00:18:24,791 --> 00:18:26,668
How could he…

197
00:18:28,420 --> 00:18:30,047
Then what was plan B?

198
00:18:32,341 --> 00:18:33,175
My sneakers.

199
00:18:44,269 --> 00:18:47,940
My sneakers were set to instantly upload
whatever they filmed to my cloud drive.

200
00:18:48,023 --> 00:18:51,443
But when I tried to access the drive
earlier from my phone, I couldn't.

201
00:18:51,526 --> 00:18:53,612
I think they hacked my account too.

202
00:18:53,695 --> 00:18:54,988
Then what do we do?

203
00:18:55,489 --> 00:18:56,615
There is a way.

204
00:18:56,698 --> 00:19:00,953
I had the cameras in my watch and sneakers
synced to my laptop.

205
00:19:01,036 --> 00:19:04,581
So the footage should be saved
on my laptop at home.

206
00:19:04,665 --> 00:19:05,499
But

207
00:19:06,083 --> 00:19:07,918
I'm scared to go home right now.

208
00:19:08,001 --> 00:19:10,963
In case Baek Sang-gil's people
might have done something to it?

209
00:19:11,713 --> 00:19:12,547
Yeah.

210
00:19:16,635 --> 00:19:18,178
So, I was wondering…

211
00:19:25,560 --> 00:19:27,980
-How did it go?
-There were no suspicious vehicles.

212
00:19:28,063 --> 00:19:31,149
And there were no bugs or cameras
around your home either.

213
00:19:31,650 --> 00:19:35,028
But there were signs that someone
had tampered with the door lock.

214
00:19:35,529 --> 00:19:36,613
-Sorry?
-Sorry?

215
00:19:37,114 --> 00:19:39,074
We did a thorough check of the place.

216
00:19:39,157 --> 00:19:40,784
It's safe, so you can go in.

217
00:19:41,618 --> 00:19:42,661
Okay, thank you.

218
00:20:12,858 --> 00:20:14,234
What? Your laptop.

219
00:20:16,278 --> 00:20:18,822
Your laptop is gone.

220
00:20:18,905 --> 00:20:21,408
Those bastards must have taken
your laptop too.

221
00:20:22,117 --> 00:20:25,704
Of course.
Baek Sang-gil is a meticulous bastard.

222
00:20:25,787 --> 00:20:26,705
So what now?

223
00:20:26,788 --> 00:20:28,498
Is it saved anywhere else?

224
00:20:30,417 --> 00:20:33,253
It's not. The memory chip in the sneakers
is the last place.

225
00:20:33,879 --> 00:20:34,796
Where are they?

226
00:20:36,631 --> 00:20:38,425
They found no viable fingerprints

227
00:20:38,508 --> 00:20:42,471
on the clothes and shoes you were wearing
when you were found.

228
00:20:43,555 --> 00:20:47,559
Why did I wear a suit with sneakers
instead of dress shoes that day?

229
00:20:47,642 --> 00:20:48,727
So unstylish.

230
00:20:53,690 --> 00:20:54,941
In Taffy Village.

231
00:20:55,025 --> 00:20:57,736
That's great. Then let's ask
that Jang Tae-ha guy for help.

232
00:20:57,819 --> 00:20:59,738
And tell him you got your memory back.

233
00:20:59,821 --> 00:21:03,617
We can't do that. If he finds out
my memory's back, he won't just stand by.

234
00:21:03,700 --> 00:21:07,204
He'll definitely try to send me somewhere
or try to protect me.

235
00:21:07,287 --> 00:21:08,830
He'd disrupt the investigation.

236
00:21:10,499 --> 00:21:12,918
I don't want to put him in more danger
because of me.

237
00:21:14,753 --> 00:21:15,837
Then what will you do?

238
00:21:28,934 --> 00:21:29,810
Chairman.

239
00:21:30,435 --> 00:21:32,354
I think Prosecutor Go is in Korea.

240
00:21:33,688 --> 00:21:34,523
What?

241
00:21:34,606 --> 00:21:38,151
I confirmed that no ships left the port
overnight except that cargo ship.

242
00:21:38,235 --> 00:21:42,364
And some of our men saw her
leaving the port on a motorcycle.

243
00:22:07,472 --> 00:22:10,308
Why did you come
when Prosecutor Go isn't even here?

244
00:22:10,392 --> 00:22:14,646
You had the nerve to hide Prosecutor Go
and thought I'd just sit still?

245
00:22:17,107 --> 00:22:19,151
You must be upset
about your dear disciple,

246
00:22:20,318 --> 00:22:24,448
but I always make sure to repay my debts,
favors, and grudges.

247
00:22:26,366 --> 00:22:30,454
Even you praised my tenacity
when I was a boxer, did you not?

248
00:22:39,921 --> 00:22:43,842
If you're going to play the "former coach"
and give me some half-baked advice…

249
00:22:49,931 --> 00:22:50,765
Can't you just

250
00:22:52,225 --> 00:22:53,477
let Tae-ha go now?

251
00:22:55,520 --> 00:22:57,230
Prosecutor Go has lost her memory,

252
00:22:58,273 --> 00:23:00,066
so she can't do you any harm.

253
00:23:02,652 --> 00:23:04,571
If it's me you hate,

254
00:23:05,822 --> 00:23:07,240
then do whatever you want

255
00:23:08,783 --> 00:23:09,618
to me.

256
00:23:13,121 --> 00:23:14,372
Let Tae-ha go.

257
00:23:15,916 --> 00:23:16,791
Let him go.

258
00:23:17,417 --> 00:23:20,212
That poor boy has never lived for himself
his entire life.

259
00:23:21,713 --> 00:23:22,672
Please.

260
00:23:25,967 --> 00:23:26,927
Just leave him…

261
00:23:28,803 --> 00:23:29,804
alone now.

262
00:23:36,686 --> 00:23:37,562
I'm…

263
00:23:40,023 --> 00:23:40,857
I'm…

264
00:23:43,193 --> 00:23:44,361
begging you.

265
00:24:14,307 --> 00:24:15,267
KAITO

266
00:24:15,350 --> 00:24:17,686
I told you,
I spoke with Kaito on the phone.

267
00:24:18,270 --> 00:24:20,564
He said the boat departed safely.

268
00:24:21,064 --> 00:24:24,192
But… I still haven't heard from him, so…

269
00:24:25,360 --> 00:24:26,611
No news is good news.

270
00:24:26,695 --> 00:24:29,573
He'll call when everything's settled.

271
00:24:29,656 --> 00:24:31,866
Get some rest. That's it.

272
00:24:36,413 --> 00:24:37,247
You're up?

273
00:24:38,248 --> 00:24:41,376
-What took you so long at the store?
-Did you stop by somewhere?

274
00:24:41,960 --> 00:24:42,794
Yeah, the bathroom.

275
00:24:45,589 --> 00:24:48,800
Hey, don't worry about others
going to the bathroom.

276
00:24:48,883 --> 00:24:50,594
Worry about yourself.

277
00:24:51,386 --> 00:24:54,514
You're a healthy young man,
not an old man.

278
00:24:55,140 --> 00:24:56,975
What are you doing in a hospital bed?

279
00:24:58,101 --> 00:25:00,437
That's why I'm going home now.

280
00:25:00,520 --> 00:25:02,522
-Goodness.
-Already?

281
00:25:03,815 --> 00:25:06,234
Hey, I didn't mean it like that.

282
00:25:07,027 --> 00:25:10,447
I'm really fine.
There's nothing to do here anyway.

283
00:25:10,530 --> 00:25:12,616
You should recover more…

284
00:25:13,450 --> 00:25:15,368
Stay a bit longer.

285
00:25:15,452 --> 00:25:16,870
-No, I…
-I'm fine.

286
00:25:18,204 --> 00:25:19,664
That's not what I meant.

287
00:25:20,165 --> 00:25:21,416
-Watch your step.
-Careful.

288
00:25:21,499 --> 00:25:23,168
I'll go check Tae-ha's room.

289
00:25:23,251 --> 00:25:26,421
I said stay a bit longer.
Why were you in such a rush to leave?

290
00:25:26,504 --> 00:25:28,214
Should he lie down?

291
00:25:29,007 --> 00:25:30,592
-Hold on.
-Are you okay?

292
00:25:34,596 --> 00:25:36,681
-Grandma.
-Ma'am, you're here?

293
00:25:38,350 --> 00:25:40,852
-Ma'am.
-Ma'am, please.

294
00:25:40,935 --> 00:25:43,855
Tae-ha's condition right now is…

295
00:25:44,356 --> 00:25:45,440
Ma'am, please.

296
00:25:46,316 --> 00:25:52,614
How much more of an inconsiderate
grandmother do you want me to be?

297
00:25:54,115 --> 00:25:56,493
I heard you didn't go because of me.

298
00:25:57,827 --> 00:25:59,579
You like her so much,

299
00:25:59,663 --> 00:26:03,208
but you didn't go
because of my illness again.

300
00:26:04,876 --> 00:26:07,629
How do you expect me to live?

301
00:26:08,630 --> 00:26:11,299
This grandmother,
who held back her grandson twice…

302
00:26:11,925 --> 00:26:15,095
How can I continue to live
with this shame?

303
00:26:19,015 --> 00:26:22,477
And you? How are you going to live?

304
00:26:23,103 --> 00:26:26,231
You let the girl you love
more than your own life go off on her own.

305
00:26:26,731 --> 00:26:29,109
How are you going to live?

306
00:26:35,824 --> 00:26:36,991
Grandma.

307
00:26:38,493 --> 00:26:40,286
It's okay, Grandma.

308
00:26:41,830 --> 00:26:43,748
I can live just fine

309
00:26:45,125 --> 00:26:46,751
even without her.

310
00:26:50,630 --> 00:26:52,757
I'll live just fine.

311
00:26:55,176 --> 00:26:56,553
My poor baby. My baby.

312
00:26:56,636 --> 00:26:59,597
What am I going to do, my baby?

313
00:27:07,814 --> 00:27:09,899
Will you really be okay alone?

314
00:27:10,567 --> 00:27:12,235
Don't worry and go to work.

315
00:27:12,318 --> 00:27:16,156
The security company confirmed it's safe,
and Baek Sang-gil thinks I went to Japan.

316
00:27:16,239 --> 00:27:19,033
So it's actually safer here right now.

317
00:27:20,910 --> 00:27:24,164
Okay. Call me right away
if anything happens.

318
00:27:24,748 --> 00:27:25,582
Okay.

319
00:27:29,210 --> 00:27:30,503
Thank you, Hyo-jin.

320
00:27:31,212 --> 00:27:32,213
Don't be silly.

321
00:27:35,383 --> 00:27:36,551
Don't come out barefoot.

322
00:27:36,634 --> 00:27:37,719
It's okay.

323
00:27:40,138 --> 00:27:41,097
Go inside.

324
00:27:41,181 --> 00:27:43,141
-Okay.
-See you!

325
00:27:55,320 --> 00:27:58,907
They say you don't know when someone
comes, but you know when they leave.

326
00:27:58,990 --> 00:28:01,785
The entire village has gone so quiet

327
00:28:01,868 --> 00:28:05,413
all because Eun-sae has gone.

328
00:28:06,706 --> 00:28:09,584
I wonder if she has arrived safely
in Japan yet.

329
00:28:11,628 --> 00:28:14,172
Stop it, you two.

330
00:28:14,964 --> 00:28:17,592
Why are you thinking about someone
who's gone?

331
00:28:20,970 --> 00:28:26,810
Have you already forgotten me?

332
00:28:28,520 --> 00:28:30,355
Leaving only longing behind…

333
00:28:30,438 --> 00:28:32,398
Light pink roses.

334
00:28:32,482 --> 00:28:35,276
Have you really forgotten me?

335
00:28:35,777 --> 00:28:37,070
They're so pretty.

336
00:28:37,570 --> 00:28:39,113
They were her favorite.

337
00:28:44,702 --> 00:28:47,914
We had so much fun at karaoke.

338
00:28:55,588 --> 00:28:58,842
And she fought like a trooper.

339
00:29:00,510 --> 00:29:03,763
It's no good if it won't work!
Then I guess we should call it a day.

340
00:29:04,264 --> 00:29:07,058
It was such a comfort,
having that feisty hen in my corner.

341
00:29:07,141 --> 00:29:11,813
Oh, what am I to do when I miss you so?

342
00:29:13,481 --> 00:29:18,736
My longing for you only grows

343
00:29:33,459 --> 00:29:34,961
BREAKFAST, LUNCH, DINNER

344
00:30:03,197 --> 00:30:06,993
Easy. Wait, the cushions.

345
00:30:08,453 --> 00:30:10,246
You can go now. I'm fine.

346
00:30:10,330 --> 00:30:11,664
No, it's okay.

347
00:30:11,748 --> 00:30:13,124
I should be here to help you.

348
00:30:13,207 --> 00:30:16,544
You're not well, so it must be hard
for you to wash up alone too.

349
00:30:17,670 --> 00:30:19,672
Even so, you shouldn't be the one
washing me.

350
00:30:24,427 --> 00:30:26,679
-Go now before it gets more awkward.
-Okay.

351
00:30:27,180 --> 00:30:28,014
Okay, then.

352
00:30:28,598 --> 00:30:31,059
Call me if you need anything urgently.

353
00:30:31,142 --> 00:30:32,894
I'll always be one step behind you.

354
00:30:34,062 --> 00:30:34,896
Okay.

355
00:30:36,105 --> 00:30:37,482
Okay, good.

356
00:30:40,109 --> 00:30:40,944
Gang-rok.

357
00:30:41,027 --> 00:30:43,154
Yes? Yes, sir.

358
00:30:45,782 --> 00:30:47,158
You should be careful.

359
00:30:49,869 --> 00:30:54,374
Baek Sang-gil knows that you're here
and that you helped me.

360
00:30:54,457 --> 00:30:57,543
Well, why would he care about
someone like me?

361
00:30:58,294 --> 00:30:59,295
Don't worry.

362
00:30:59,921 --> 00:31:03,466
I might not be as good as you,
but I'm still a pretty good fight…

363
00:31:07,053 --> 00:31:09,347
Who are you? Who do you work for, damn it!

364
00:31:09,847 --> 00:31:12,058
Sir, I've still got it.

365
00:31:12,850 --> 00:31:13,810
Don't worry.

366
00:31:14,310 --> 00:31:15,395
Please rest.

367
00:31:20,400 --> 00:31:23,069
Sir, if anything happens,
please contact me immediately.

368
00:32:01,733 --> 00:32:02,734
Good morning.

369
00:32:57,413 --> 00:32:59,791
She must have arrived safely, right?

370
00:33:00,708 --> 00:33:03,377
I wonder if she'll find some comfort
in living there.

371
00:33:04,337 --> 00:33:06,839
This place is so beautiful.

372
00:33:06,923 --> 00:33:10,259
I bet living somewhere like this
would feel like a dream.

373
00:33:20,186 --> 00:33:22,313
I hope she's not having too hard a time.

374
00:33:23,940 --> 00:33:24,941
Go Eun-sae.

375
00:33:26,275 --> 00:33:27,985
That's not her name.

376
00:33:33,574 --> 00:33:34,784
Her name is Blessing.

377
00:33:35,409 --> 00:33:38,079
I chose it as it's a blessing
for her to have settled here.

378
00:33:38,162 --> 00:33:39,163
What…

379
00:33:39,914 --> 00:33:40,748
What happened?

380
00:33:41,707 --> 00:33:42,583
Why are you here?

381
00:33:45,461 --> 00:33:46,420
"What happened?"

382
00:33:46,504 --> 00:33:50,133
After doing something so huge to me,
how can you ask what happened?

383
00:33:51,217 --> 00:33:53,261
I was so scared, I could've died.

384
00:33:54,971 --> 00:33:56,597
Man, this is crazy.

385
00:33:57,515 --> 00:33:59,350
Why didn't you go to Japan?

386
00:33:59,433 --> 00:34:00,643
Why would I go to Japan?

387
00:34:01,227 --> 00:34:04,480
Stowaway? Why would I have to stow away?
I didn't do anything wrong.

388
00:34:04,564 --> 00:34:06,482
Because you'd be safe that way.

389
00:34:06,566 --> 00:34:08,526
I can be safe without going.

390
00:34:08,609 --> 00:34:09,735
I can just

391
00:34:11,070 --> 00:34:12,280
break up with Jang Tae-ha.

392
00:34:15,408 --> 00:34:17,285
-What?
-Why are you so surprised?

393
00:34:17,368 --> 00:34:19,704
You knew I hated gangsters.
If you were going back,

394
00:34:19,787 --> 00:34:21,455
you should've prepared to lose me.

395
00:34:25,710 --> 00:34:29,547
The reason you sent me away was
that you went back to being a gangster.

396
00:34:31,382 --> 00:34:35,511
So if I ended things with you,
wouldn't I be safe?

397
00:34:38,723 --> 00:34:41,601
Even if that's true,
you have nowhere to go right now.

398
00:34:41,684 --> 00:34:42,810
I'll go to a facility.

399
00:34:42,894 --> 00:34:46,230
And we're strangers now,
so don't ask me any more questions.

400
00:34:55,698 --> 00:34:56,574
Did…

401
00:34:58,701 --> 00:35:00,620
some of your memory

402
00:35:01,245 --> 00:35:02,538
come back?

403
00:35:04,582 --> 00:35:07,585
No. What, I can't break up with you
if my memory hasn't returned?

404
00:35:09,170 --> 00:35:11,881
I came here to say we're breaking up,
and I'll be fine.

405
00:35:11,964 --> 00:35:15,343
Thanks for taking care of me until now.
I'll just take my things and leave.

406
00:35:26,854 --> 00:35:28,064
What…

407
00:35:29,398 --> 00:35:30,858
Wait, what…

408
00:35:32,485 --> 00:35:35,363
Where are all my things?

409
00:35:36,322 --> 00:35:38,574
I sent everything to Japan yesterday.

410
00:35:38,658 --> 00:35:39,617
What?

411
00:35:39,700 --> 00:35:43,371
I asked Mr. Hong to send your things
after we left.

412
00:35:43,454 --> 00:35:46,040
But why… How could you…

413
00:35:47,833 --> 00:35:49,877
Call and ask them to send it back
right away.

414
00:35:49,961 --> 00:35:52,088
Something important is in there.

415
00:35:52,171 --> 00:35:53,422
-Hurry.
-Okay.

416
00:35:53,506 --> 00:35:54,423
Hurry.

417
00:35:58,552 --> 00:35:59,637
What did they say?

418
00:35:59,720 --> 00:36:03,224
If they send it back right away,
it should arrive by tomorrow afternoon.

419
00:36:03,307 --> 00:36:04,267
Tomorrow afternoon?

420
00:36:05,351 --> 00:36:06,769
What do I do?

421
00:36:14,402 --> 00:36:16,988
I guess I have no choice but to

422
00:36:17,571 --> 00:36:18,739
stay here tonight.

423
00:36:21,325 --> 00:36:23,786
The package won't get here until tomorrow.

424
00:36:23,869 --> 00:36:27,206
It'd be impractical to go to Seoul today
and come back tomorrow.

425
00:36:27,290 --> 00:36:30,459
You must've already said you want
to break up. How tragically funny.

426
00:36:32,044 --> 00:36:33,004
Yeah, I know.

427
00:36:33,087 --> 00:36:34,755
Well, I guess you have no choice.

428
00:36:35,339 --> 00:36:36,966
Enjoy the sleepover.

429
00:36:39,218 --> 00:36:41,721
I'm with Go Eun-sae now.
Call me when you see this.

430
00:36:50,771 --> 00:36:52,606
Don't you dare try to ship me off again.

431
00:36:53,482 --> 00:36:57,278
I'm not someone who obediently goes
wherever you tell me to go.

432
00:36:59,530 --> 00:37:01,240
You were never particularly

433
00:37:01,907 --> 00:37:02,742
obedient.

434
00:37:08,748 --> 00:37:11,751
It seems like you really let yourself go
while I was gone.

435
00:37:12,626 --> 00:37:13,627
What?

436
00:37:19,008 --> 00:37:20,301
I just left the hospital.

437
00:37:25,639 --> 00:37:27,141
I can't believe you.

438
00:37:32,438 --> 00:37:34,982
What are you doing? Go take a shower.

439
00:37:37,276 --> 00:37:39,195
-Are you okay?
-Yeah.

440
00:37:39,278 --> 00:37:40,488
I'm sorry.

441
00:37:40,571 --> 00:37:42,698
You're more hurt than I thought.

442
00:37:45,284 --> 00:37:46,118
Then

443
00:37:46,869 --> 00:37:49,038
you mustn't be able to shower on your own.

444
00:37:53,042 --> 00:37:53,876
Right?

445
00:38:00,508 --> 00:38:01,675
There's nothing to wash.

446
00:38:03,010 --> 00:38:04,345
But I have a lot of hair.

447
00:38:05,096 --> 00:38:06,722
I meant that you have a small head.

448
00:38:14,146 --> 00:38:16,399
I can dry it myself.

449
00:38:16,482 --> 00:38:17,983
Just stay put.

450
00:38:31,205 --> 00:38:33,958
I can just break up with Jang Tae-ha.

451
00:38:38,462 --> 00:38:40,506
Now you look better.

452
00:38:42,216 --> 00:38:44,427
Was I that hideous to look at?

453
00:38:44,510 --> 00:38:45,553
Yes.

454
00:38:54,770 --> 00:38:58,023
-Which facility are you going to?
-I told you not to ask.

455
00:38:58,524 --> 00:38:59,650
I told you, we broke up.

456
00:39:00,943 --> 00:39:02,069
We can still stay in--

457
00:39:02,153 --> 00:39:03,737
You've never washed her, right?

458
00:39:04,321 --> 00:39:05,156
What?

459
00:39:07,199 --> 00:39:08,033
No.

460
00:39:09,160 --> 00:39:10,411
I knew it.

461
00:39:10,995 --> 00:39:14,915
Everyone in this house ends up so dirty
if I'm not around.

462
00:39:16,917 --> 00:39:18,252
Come on, follow me.

463
00:39:25,176 --> 00:39:27,386
I wonder if she'll turn into a white dog.

464
00:39:36,187 --> 00:39:37,480
-My eyes.
-It's in your eyes?

465
00:39:37,563 --> 00:39:39,023
-The soap…
-Are you okay?

466
00:40:04,507 --> 00:40:05,549
Are you okay?

467
00:40:12,306 --> 00:40:13,140
Ma'am!

468
00:40:14,808 --> 00:40:18,062
We stopped by
because we heard you were here.

469
00:40:18,145 --> 00:40:21,565
Yeah, so we came in a hurry.

470
00:40:22,107 --> 00:40:24,735
But… should we come back later?

471
00:40:24,818 --> 00:40:25,653
No…

472
00:40:25,736 --> 00:40:27,905
Are you feeling okay, Eun-sae?

473
00:40:28,405 --> 00:40:32,117
You all knew I was going far away,
but you kept it from me.

474
00:40:33,160 --> 00:40:35,663
But what happened?

475
00:40:35,746 --> 00:40:37,456
Where were you all this time?

476
00:40:37,540 --> 00:40:39,667
Jang Tae-ha can fill you in.

477
00:40:41,210 --> 00:40:42,294
Where are you going?

478
00:40:43,337 --> 00:40:45,422
I'm going to get something for our dinner.

479
00:40:45,506 --> 00:40:48,384
Don't follow me, Jang Tae-ha.
Explain to them what's going on.

480
00:40:49,176 --> 00:40:50,594
And catch Blessing and bathe her.

481
00:40:56,016 --> 00:40:57,142
Hey, what the heck?

482
00:40:57,226 --> 00:40:59,645
Why is she suddenly so cold to you?

483
00:41:03,315 --> 00:41:04,149
What happened?

484
00:41:06,860 --> 00:41:09,363
You should have told me
if you knew she hadn't gone.

485
00:41:09,863 --> 00:41:11,448
That was because

486
00:41:12,032 --> 00:41:16,245
we knew you'd go looking for her
even though you were in no state to.

487
00:41:16,328 --> 00:41:21,333
But I'm really glad
Eun-sae showed up safe and sound.

488
00:41:22,501 --> 00:41:28,382
But she can't stay in Taffy Village
anymore, right?

489
00:41:29,758 --> 00:41:33,971
Since Baek Sang-gil knows about it,
it's not as safe as it used to be.

490
00:41:34,054 --> 00:41:36,932
I asked Kaito to find out
when the next stowaway boat will leave,

491
00:41:37,016 --> 00:41:38,726
but it'll take a while.

492
00:41:38,809 --> 00:41:40,811
And it won't be easy
to convince Go Eun-sae.

493
00:41:41,770 --> 00:41:42,896
On that note,

494
00:41:42,980 --> 00:41:46,609
did you happen to see an odd suit
and sneakers when you packed her stuff?

495
00:41:48,027 --> 00:41:49,737
-Did you see them?
-No.

496
00:41:49,820 --> 00:41:50,988
Did you see them?

497
00:41:51,071 --> 00:41:52,531
Odd?

498
00:41:53,032 --> 00:41:55,576
I think the plan B evidence
Baek Sang-gil is looking for

499
00:41:55,659 --> 00:41:58,829
is in the outfit Go Eun-sae was wearing
at the time of the incident.

500
00:41:58,912 --> 00:42:03,208
Somewhere like the buttons on the suit,
the belt, or the sneakers.

501
00:42:03,292 --> 00:42:04,918
That makes sense.

502
00:42:06,378 --> 00:42:09,298
We'll have to look for that first
when her stuff comes back.

503
00:42:10,049 --> 00:42:11,675
If we find that evidence,

504
00:42:11,759 --> 00:42:13,719
we may be able to keep her safe

505
00:42:14,887 --> 00:42:16,388
without having to send her away.

506
00:42:21,268 --> 00:42:24,980
LETTER OF RESIGNATION
NAME: MIN SU-JI

507
00:42:28,067 --> 00:42:30,486
Maybe hating me
will make it hurt a little less.

508
00:42:47,294 --> 00:42:48,420
What are you doing?

509
00:42:48,504 --> 00:42:50,756
You asked to see me,
and now you've gone quiet?

510
00:42:50,839 --> 00:42:51,715
What?

511
00:42:52,883 --> 00:42:54,009
Right, I…

512
00:42:56,095 --> 00:42:59,473
I… realized something recently.

513
00:43:00,224 --> 00:43:02,935
I'd been standing in a field of flowers.

514
00:43:03,644 --> 00:43:06,522
Some people are forced to break up
even when they love someone

515
00:43:07,690 --> 00:43:09,149
enough to risk their lives.

516
00:43:10,609 --> 00:43:14,822
Even fighting over our pride like this
feels like a luxury.

517
00:43:15,572 --> 00:43:16,407
I wanted to say…

518
00:43:20,369 --> 00:43:21,578
I'm sorry for everything.

519
00:43:23,205 --> 00:43:25,374
For the times I didn't mean to,

520
00:43:25,457 --> 00:43:30,337
and the times I did mean to hurt you
the way I did.

521
00:43:30,838 --> 00:43:31,964
I'm sorry for everything.

522
00:43:33,882 --> 00:43:34,717
And…

523
00:43:36,927 --> 00:43:38,929
I really liked you a lot, Min Su-ji.

524
00:43:40,806 --> 00:43:43,642
I actually don't really like yulmu tea.

525
00:43:43,726 --> 00:43:46,270
But when I ordered it,

526
00:43:46,353 --> 00:43:50,858
I was able to see you some more,
so I ordered several cups.

527
00:43:55,529 --> 00:43:56,572
Here's your yulmu tea.

528
00:43:57,823 --> 00:43:58,657
Thanks.

529
00:43:59,158 --> 00:44:01,326
I just love yulmu tea.

530
00:44:08,792 --> 00:44:11,044
When I dated you,
someone who I liked so much,

531
00:44:11,545 --> 00:44:12,421
I really felt like

532
00:44:13,297 --> 00:44:15,048
I had the whole world.

533
00:44:16,592 --> 00:44:19,178
But people are so fickle and petty.

534
00:44:20,012 --> 00:44:21,346
I forgot all about that.

535
00:44:23,599 --> 00:44:24,558
So now I'll

536
00:44:25,851 --> 00:44:26,852
respect your decision.

537
00:44:27,978 --> 00:44:30,063
You can stop coming to the clinic.

538
00:44:32,357 --> 00:44:33,567
An Gi-jun…

539
00:44:33,650 --> 00:44:36,361
And, as you wanted,

540
00:44:37,362 --> 00:44:40,491
let's break up now.

541
00:44:47,831 --> 00:44:49,958
I'll get going, then.

542
00:45:06,350 --> 00:45:10,145
This isn't really
your type of cuisine, is it?

543
00:45:11,063 --> 00:45:13,398
I guess my taste buds changed
after I almost died.

544
00:45:13,482 --> 00:45:14,650
Everyone, dig in.

545
00:45:14,733 --> 00:45:17,277
-Okay.
-Thank you for the food.

546
00:45:17,361 --> 00:45:19,947
-I don't know what to start with.
-This looks good.

547
00:45:20,030 --> 00:45:23,242
-I've never tried this.
-I can't even make this.

548
00:45:25,702 --> 00:45:27,246
You're in your twenties, Gang-rok.

549
00:45:27,830 --> 00:45:32,000
They say black chicken legs are good
for people in their thirties and older.

550
00:45:32,668 --> 00:45:34,711
I guess that means I qualify.

551
00:45:34,795 --> 00:45:36,463
Yeah, you do.

552
00:45:36,547 --> 00:45:37,464
Abalone.

553
00:45:42,553 --> 00:45:44,096
The abalone smells a bit fishy.

554
00:45:45,013 --> 00:45:47,266
You should eat this, Jang Tae-ha.

555
00:45:50,769 --> 00:45:52,729
You should eat some too.

556
00:45:53,313 --> 00:45:54,606
Yeah, thanks.

557
00:45:54,690 --> 00:45:56,650
I can eat the chicken neck, right?

558
00:45:57,609 --> 00:45:58,902
Eat some shrimp too.

559
00:45:59,611 --> 00:46:01,154
Long time no see, shrimp.

560
00:46:01,238 --> 00:46:03,699
There's a lot of kimchi. Eat up.

561
00:46:03,782 --> 00:46:06,076
Wow, so much kimchi.

562
00:46:11,415 --> 00:46:12,916
I ate, but I'm still hungry.

563
00:46:19,298 --> 00:46:23,552
Didn't it seem like the menu was
for Tae-ha's health and recovery?

564
00:46:23,635 --> 00:46:24,469
Yeah.

565
00:46:24,970 --> 00:46:27,097
And if they're about to break up,

566
00:46:27,180 --> 00:46:29,850
isn't it weird that she said
she'd sleep over?

567
00:46:30,726 --> 00:46:31,643
She has our place.

568
00:46:31,727 --> 00:46:33,770
And the S.E.S ladies' places too.

569
00:46:34,271 --> 00:46:35,689
She didn't have to…

570
00:46:35,772 --> 00:46:36,982
That's what I'm saying.

571
00:46:38,317 --> 00:46:39,151
What's going on?

572
00:46:39,902 --> 00:46:42,529
Seemingly distant, but still close…

573
00:46:42,613 --> 00:46:44,781
This sticky feeling.

574
00:46:49,661 --> 00:46:50,996
Take that off now.

575
00:46:56,209 --> 00:46:57,044
Do what?

576
00:46:57,127 --> 00:46:59,296
We have to disinfect the wound.

577
00:46:59,379 --> 00:47:01,381
Mr. Hong said to make sure to do it.

578
00:47:06,511 --> 00:47:07,346
Right.

579
00:47:07,846 --> 00:47:09,640
I can do this myself.

580
00:47:10,849 --> 00:47:13,310
Is your arm two meters long or something?

581
00:47:13,393 --> 00:47:15,562
How will you disinfect
a wound on your back?

582
00:47:15,646 --> 00:47:17,022
Really, it's okay.

583
00:47:17,105 --> 00:47:19,149
Hurry up.

584
00:47:39,920 --> 00:47:41,588
You said you were a good fighter.

585
00:47:42,297 --> 00:47:43,256
That was a total lie.

586
00:47:43,340 --> 00:47:45,467
You got hurt badly.

587
00:47:47,135 --> 00:47:51,014
I guess you were so shocked
that you didn't see it properly.

588
00:47:51,932 --> 00:47:53,850
I took on almost 20 guys from the start.

589
00:47:53,934 --> 00:47:55,185
Zip it.

590
00:48:08,991 --> 00:48:11,118
Anyway, thank you for saving me.

591
00:48:12,536 --> 00:48:17,624
Even if we're breaking up,
I'm still grateful.

592
00:48:25,298 --> 00:48:27,426
While I was living with you…

593
00:48:29,469 --> 00:48:31,346
I felt so secure.

594
00:48:33,390 --> 00:48:37,310
No matter how dangerous things got,
I wasn't afraid.

595
00:48:39,646 --> 00:48:44,568
Even the world's tallest mountain
wouldn't have stood taller than your back.

596
00:48:52,993 --> 00:48:55,245
Thank you so much

597
00:48:56,997 --> 00:48:58,790
for risking your life to save me.

598
00:49:27,819 --> 00:49:29,529
Just wait a little bit.

599
00:49:30,781 --> 00:49:33,200
I'll protect you now.

600
00:49:44,294 --> 00:49:45,670
I promise I will.

601
00:50:27,921 --> 00:50:29,714
-Touch.
-Keep your guard up.

602
00:50:29,798 --> 00:50:31,174
37 YEARS AGO

603
00:50:31,258 --> 00:50:32,425
Move back.

604
00:50:34,010 --> 00:50:35,220
Keep your guard up.

605
00:50:35,303 --> 00:50:36,304
Hello, sir!

606
00:50:37,305 --> 00:50:39,266
Nice to meet you. I'm Hong Do-yeop.

607
00:50:41,268 --> 00:50:42,811
I'm Baek Sang-gil. I just joined.

608
00:50:43,311 --> 00:50:45,605
I've been a fan since the Asian Games.

609
00:50:46,106 --> 00:50:47,607
You're my role model.

610
00:50:48,775 --> 00:50:49,651
I see.

611
00:51:11,339 --> 00:51:12,465
You lost.

612
00:51:38,241 --> 00:51:40,535
Has it been about 30 years or so?

613
00:51:41,036 --> 00:51:44,623
I think you had about a dozen bottles here
back then too.

614
00:51:46,291 --> 00:51:47,918
You have a good memory.

615
00:51:52,881 --> 00:51:54,257
Back then, I…

616
00:51:56,384 --> 00:51:57,719
really felt like shit.

617
00:52:00,805 --> 00:52:03,808
I thought drinking hard liquor
would help me feel better.

618
00:52:07,312 --> 00:52:08,188
What is it?

619
00:52:09,522 --> 00:52:11,733
Angry about something today too?
Like back then?

620
00:52:16,196 --> 00:52:17,030
Angry?

621
00:52:18,823 --> 00:52:21,117
It's not anger. What should I call it?

622
00:52:22,661 --> 00:52:24,371
It feels filthier than that.

623
00:52:31,628 --> 00:52:33,171
A filthy sense of defeat.

624
00:52:35,257 --> 00:52:38,635
It's been a long time
since I felt this filthy feeling.

625
00:52:42,389 --> 00:52:45,100
Back then, I didn't know what to do
about this feeling.

626
00:52:48,186 --> 00:52:49,187
I think I know now.

627
00:52:54,234 --> 00:52:56,111
One thing can cover up a sense of defeat.

628
00:52:58,905 --> 00:52:59,823
Winning.

629
00:53:04,494 --> 00:53:05,662
This time…

630
00:53:10,625 --> 00:53:12,210
I must win no matter what.

631
00:53:28,018 --> 00:53:30,645
RETURNED

632
00:53:39,112 --> 00:53:40,363
Look.

633
00:53:40,447 --> 00:53:43,783
I have a lot of underwear in here.
Can you leave?

634
00:53:44,826 --> 00:53:46,119
Right, sure.

635
00:54:21,821 --> 00:54:23,323
I found it.

636
00:54:25,033 --> 00:54:28,328
When you get there,
please let me know her destination.

637
00:54:28,411 --> 00:54:30,789
Goodness, if you're so worried,

638
00:54:30,872 --> 00:54:32,832
why don't you take her there yourself?

639
00:54:32,916 --> 00:54:35,418
I want to, but she insists
she doesn't want me to.

640
00:54:35,502 --> 00:54:37,837
-Okay.
-Thank you.

641
00:54:46,429 --> 00:54:47,597
I'll get going now.

642
00:54:53,269 --> 00:54:55,021
Take care of yourself.

643
00:54:56,481 --> 00:54:57,482
Go Eun-sae.

644
00:55:00,735 --> 00:55:02,529
Even though you said we're breaking up…

645
00:55:04,656 --> 00:55:05,740
I still like you.

646
00:55:08,910 --> 00:55:10,203
So if you're ever in danger

647
00:55:10,787 --> 00:55:11,704
or scared,

648
00:55:13,373 --> 00:55:14,541
or if anything happens…

649
00:55:17,168 --> 00:55:18,670
If you need help,

650
00:55:19,879 --> 00:55:21,464
feel free to call me anytime.

651
00:55:21,548 --> 00:55:22,632
It's okay to do that.

652
00:55:32,225 --> 00:55:33,935
I will call when I get there.

653
00:55:36,104 --> 00:55:39,023
But not you. I'll call Jeong-hwa.

654
00:56:04,299 --> 00:56:06,551
Jang Tae-ha, you seriously…

655
00:56:12,640 --> 00:56:15,602
She never took out that suit
or the sneakers while she was here.

656
00:56:16,728 --> 00:56:18,313
But she decided to take them?

657
00:56:19,856 --> 00:56:21,858
Call and ask them to send it back
right away.

658
00:56:21,941 --> 00:56:23,485
Something important is in there.

659
00:56:29,282 --> 00:56:30,325
HONG DO-YEOP

660
00:56:31,034 --> 00:56:31,868
Yes?

661
00:56:31,951 --> 00:56:34,287
Are you with Gang-rok by any chance?

662
00:56:34,370 --> 00:56:35,497
I'm not. Why?

663
00:56:35,580 --> 00:56:40,293
I wanted to eat with him, but I haven't
been able to reach him for a while.

664
00:56:40,376 --> 00:56:41,836
I'll go to his place.

665
00:56:41,920 --> 00:56:43,213
Okay, do that.

666
00:56:44,088 --> 00:56:45,507
Gang-rok!

667
00:56:47,759 --> 00:56:48,927
Kim Gang-rok.

668
00:56:53,014 --> 00:56:54,474
Where did he go?

669
00:57:06,236 --> 00:57:08,571
Baek Sang-gil knows that you're here

670
00:57:08,655 --> 00:57:10,448
and that you helped me.

671
00:57:11,115 --> 00:57:12,450
You should be careful.

672
00:57:23,127 --> 00:57:25,755
KIM GANG-ROK
MY CURRENT LOCATION

673
00:57:48,695 --> 00:57:50,071
Hey, watch out!

674
00:57:56,286 --> 00:57:57,579
Is this bastard crazy?

675
00:58:03,376 --> 00:58:05,336
Hey, you bastard!

676
00:58:13,136 --> 00:58:14,721
You son of a bitch!

677
00:58:17,515 --> 00:58:19,726
Gang-rok, stay with me.

678
00:58:20,310 --> 00:58:21,352
Gang-rok!

679
00:58:24,355 --> 00:58:26,649
I told you I'm a good fighter.

680
00:58:27,692 --> 00:58:28,818
Why did you come here?

681
00:58:43,499 --> 00:58:44,334
Hold on to me.

682
00:59:00,892 --> 00:59:01,768
Hang in there.

683
00:59:01,851 --> 00:59:03,561
Just until we get to the hospital.

684
01:02:01,280 --> 01:02:03,449
Jeong-hwa!

685
01:02:04,116 --> 01:02:05,117
Jeong-hwa!

686
01:02:05,993 --> 01:02:07,286
Jeong-hwa!

687
01:02:07,370 --> 01:02:10,039
Damn it! Jeong-hwa!

688
01:02:21,467 --> 01:02:22,593
Jeong-hwa!

689
01:02:29,350 --> 01:02:30,268
Jeong-hwa!

690
01:02:56,168 --> 01:02:58,254
My Jeong-hwa.

691
01:03:11,017 --> 01:03:12,685
OUR STICKY LOVE

692
01:03:59,315 --> 01:04:03,277
Subtitle translation by: Jimin Choi

